    },
    {
      "id": "n-head",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 924,
      "y": 2364,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 20,
      "strokeColor": "#1c1e26",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "roughness": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "N",
        "lane3"
      ],
      "seed": 3402,
      "text": "What has to be built, and what it costs",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "autoResize": false,
      "index": "a234",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790251001522,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What has to be built, and what it costs",
      "lineHeight": 1.3333333333333333
    },
    {
      "id": "n-body",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 924,
      "y": 2398,
      "width": 1490,
      "height": 220,
      "strokeColor": "#4b5563",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "roughness": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "N",
        "lane3"
      ],
      "seed": 3403,
      "text": "The browser lane needs nothing from the service: the code purchase runs exactly as it ships, the browser mints the code and sends only its SHA-256, and the only reason the buyer\nnever sees one is that the link carries it instead of the screen. The store lane is the part that does need service work - purchaseBadge has to accept a store receipt and verify it,\nand no provider adapter for that exists today.\n\nThe page needs three things: read ?app and start at Choose your badge; at the end, try the deep link and offer Return to SimpleX with Show code under it; and for #app=desktop,\nkeep showing codeIssued as it does now.\n\nThe app needs: Buy in browser without its confirm alert; a handler for the new link; A6, a spinner around the existing apiRedeemBadgeCode; on desktop, opening Redeem code alongside\nthe browser; and for the store lane, B4's checkout and the two BadgeState outcomes behind B5.\n\nWhat it costs: the app cannot show a price before sending the buyer out, because it has no catalog - Buy in browser is a leap into a page. And the code still exists, so it can be\nintercepted, screenshotted from the backup button, or pasted somewhere else. Hidden is not the same as absent.",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "autoResize": false,
      "index": "a235",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790251001522,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The browser lane needs nothing from the service: the code purchase runs exactly as it ships, the browser mints the code and sends only its SHA-256, and the only reason the buyer\nnever sees one is that the link carries it instead of the screen. The store lane is the part that does need service work - purchaseBadge has to accept a store receipt and verify it,\nand no provider adapter for that exists today.\n\nThe page needs three things: read ?app and start at Choose your badge; at the end, try the deep link and offer Return to SimpleX with Show code under it; and for #app=desktop,\nkeep showing codeIssued as it does now.\n\nThe app needs: Buy in browser without its confirm alert; a handler for the new link; A6, a spinner around the existing apiRedeemBadgeCode; on desktop, opening Redeem code alongside\nthe browser; and for the store lane, B4's checkout and the two BadgeState outcomes behind B5.\n\nWhat it costs: the app cannot show a price before sending the buyer out, because it has no catalog - Buy in browser is a leap into a page. And the code still exists, so it can be\nintercepted, screenshotted from the backup button, or pasted somewhere else. Hidden is not the same as absent.",
      "lineHeight": 2
    },
